title: Vocabulary Meta Fields
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The meta tiddler is itself the vocabulary's marker tag: its title (e.g. `vocab/markdown`) is what each marker tiddler in the vocabulary carries in its `tags` field. So no separate field declares the tag — the title is the tag.

The meta tiddler tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary>> carries:

|! Field |! Required |! Notes |! Example |
|`caption` |yes |Human-friendly name used in `;vocab=<Caption>` activation and the marker-summary header. |[[vocab/markdown]] |
|`description` |no |One-sentence summary. Surfaced in the vocab-summary ViewTemplate. |[[vocab/fountain]] |
|`version` |no |Free-form. Convention: SemVer. |[[vocab/markdown]] |
|`disable-core-rules` |no |Space-separated TW core wikirule names. Suppressed when this vocab is activated for a tiddler. |[[vocab/markdown]] |
|`front-matter` |no |`yes` opts into a `Key: Value` block at the top of any tiddler of that type. |[[vocab/fountain]] |
|`filter` |no |When set together with the `$:/tags/Filter` tag, the vocab meta also acts as a self-export bundle. |[[vocab/markdown]] |

The ''Example'' column links to a real vocab tiddler where the field is populated. Open it to see the field in context.

!! Worked example: `disable-core-rules`

[[vocab/markdown]] claims several TW core syntaxes for itself:

```
title: vocab/markdown
caption: Markdown
version: 0.4.0
disable-core-rules: strikethrough codeinline list underscore table
```

When a tiddler activates the Markdown vocab (via `;vocab=Markdown`), the listed TW core rules are removed from the parser for that tiddler only. So `~~strike~~` fires the markdown STRIKETHROUGH marker instead of TW's strikethrough; `` `x` `` fires the markdown CODE marker instead of TW's `codeinline`; `# h1` fires the markdown HEADING-1 marker instead of TW's `list` (which would otherwise treat `#` as ordered list); `__bold__` fires markdown BOLD-ALT instead of TW's underscore underline; `|a|b|` fires markdown-table instead of TW's table.

See [[$:/core/ui/ControlPanel/Parsing]] for the rule catalogue (filters: `[wikiparserrules[block]]`, `[wikiparserrules[inline]]`, `[wikiparserrules[pragma]]`).

!! Worked example: `front-matter`

''Vocab meta:'' [[vocab/fountain]] (declares `front-matter: yes`).

''Consumer tiddler:'' [[Example - Fountain screenplay]] (opens with a real `Title: / Credit: / Author:` block at the top of its source).

```
title: vocab/fountain
caption: Fountain
front-matter: yes
disable-core-rules: heading list
```

In any tiddler that activates Fountain, the engine consumes a `Key: Value` block at the top of the source (terminating at the first blank line or `===` separator) and renders it as `<div class="wltc-front-matter">` with one row per pair. Keys must start with an uppercase letter (`Title:`, `Author:`, `Credit:`). Intended for screenplay title pages and similar metadata-at-the-top conventions; not a YAML replacement (no list values, no continuation lines).

!! Worked example: `filter` (bundle self-export)

Every shipped vocab meta also carries a `filter` field and the `$:/tags/Filter` tag, so the vocab tiddler itself doubles as an export bundle:

```
title: vocab/markdown
tags: $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary $:/tags/Filter
filter: [[vocab/markdown]] [all[shadows+tiddlers]tag[vocab/markdown]]
```

Click the export button on the vocab tiddler and you get a JSON file containing the vocab meta plus every marker tagged with the vocab title. Lets a vocab travel as one self-contained file.